Input: {"question": "Who is Emil Telmányi's spouse?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 70, "text": "Title: The Harmonious Union: The Story of Emil and Anne Marie Telmányi"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 72, "end": 223, "text": "In the early 20th century, the world of art and music was abuzz with talented individuals who would leave an indelible mark on their respective fields."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 224, "end": 367, "text": "Among them were Emil Telmányi, a Hungarian violinist of exceptional skill, and Anne Marie Telmányi, a Danish painter with a unique perspective."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 368, "end": 473, "text": "Their lives, though seemingly disparate, would intersect in a beautiful union that would last a lifetime."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 474, "end": 578, "text": "Emil Telmányi, born in 1892, was a child prodigy who began his violin studies at the tender age of five."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 579, "end": 741, "text": "His talent and dedication earned him a place at the Franz Liszt Academy of Music in Budapest, where he honed his craft under the guidance of renowned instructors."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 742, "end": 883, "text": "As he matured, Emil's virtuosity on the violin took him to concert halls across Europe, earning him critical acclaim and a devoted following."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 884, "end": 974, "text": "Meanwhile, in Denmark, Anne Marie Telmányi was making a name for herself in the art world."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 975, "end": 1094, "text": "Born in 1893, she was drawn to painting from a young age and went on to study at the Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1095, "end": 1203, "text": "Her unique style, which blended elements of Expressionism and Cubism, set her apart from her contemporaries."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1204, "end": 1343, "text": "Anne Marie's artwork was met with enthusiasm by critics and collectors alike, solidifying her position as a prominent figure in Danish art."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1344, "end": 1466, "text": "The paths of these two talented individuals converged in the 1920s, when Emil Telmányi was touring Europe with his violin."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1467, "end": 1580, "text": "It was during one of his performances in Copenhagen that he met Anne Marie, who was in attendance at the concert."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1581, "end": 1719, "text": "The sparks that flew between them were not limited to the music; a deep connection was formed, and soon they found themselves inseparable."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1720, "end": 1797, "text": "Their marriage, which took place in 1925, was a union of two kindred spirits."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1798, "end": 1867, "text": "Emil and Anne Marie shared a passion for art, music, and life itself."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1868, "end": 2028, "text": "They spent their days surrounded by creativity, with Emil's violin playing and Anne Marie's painting serving as a constant source of inspiration for each other."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2029, "end": 2119, "text": "As the years passed, the Telmányis became an integral part of Copenhagen's cultural scene."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2120, "end": 2255, "text": "Their home, filled with music, art, and laughter, was a gathering place for like-minded individuals who shared their love for the arts."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 169, "text": "As the sun dipped into the Indian Ocean, casting a warm orange glow over the bustling streets of Bombay, Emil Telmányi's fingers danced across the strings of his violin."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 170, "end": 360, "text": "The sweet, melancholic notes of the Hungarian folk song \"Székely Lament\" wafted through the open windows of the Hervey's colonial bungalow, enticing the evening air with its haunting beauty."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 361, "end": 474, "text": "Inside, Dudley Hervey, resplendent in his crisp white uniform, sat entranced, his eyes fixed on the man he loved."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 475, "end": 661, "text": "It was a moment of rare tranquility in the midst of the chaotic colonial administration, where Dudley's duties as a district officer often kept him away from Emil for weeks at a stretch."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 662, "end": 763, "text": "But tonight, with the monsoon rains finally subsiding, they had stolen a few precious hours together."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 764, "end": 915, "text": "As Emil's music came to a close, Dudley rose from his chair, his face aglow with admiration, and wrapped his arms around the violinist's slender waist."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 916, "end": 994, "text": "\"My love, you are a sorcerer,\" Dudley whispered, his voice husky with emotion."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 995, "end": 1032, "text": "\"You weave magic with those strings.\""}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1033, "end": 1110, "text": "Emil's eyes sparkled with mischief as he leaned in to kiss Dudley's forehead."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1111, "end": 1160, "text": "\"And you, my dear, are the master of this domain."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1161, "end": 1222, "text": "Without you, I would be lost in this vast, bewildering land.\""}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1223, "end": 1381, "text": "As they stood there, swaying to the rhythm of their own private waltz, the sounds of the city outside receded, and all that mattered was the love they shared."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1382, "end": 1525, "text": "It was a love that had blossomed in the unlikeliest of places, amidst the dusty files and bureaucratic red tape of the colonial administration."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1526, "end": 1668, "text": "Yet, it was a love that had grown strong and resilient, a flame that burned bright despite the challenges and secrets they had to keep hidden."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "spouse", "scope": "Emil Telmányi", "claim": "Emil Telmányi's spouse is Anne Marie Telmányi.", "answer": "Anne Marie Telmányi", "quote": "Among them were Emil Telmányi, a Hungarian violinist of exceptional skill, and Anne Marie Telmányi, a Danish painter with a unique perspective. Their lives, though seemingly disparate, would intersect in a beautiful union that would last a lifetime. Emil Telmányi, born in 1892, was a child prodigy who began his violin studies at the tender age of five. His talent and dedication earned him a place at the Franz Liszt Academy of Music in Budapest, where he honed his craft under the guidance of renowned instructors. As he matured, Emil's virtuosity on the violin took him to concert halls across Europe, earning him critical acclaim and a devoted following. Meanwhile, in Denmark, Anne Marie Telmányi was making a name for herself in the art world. Born in 1893, she was drawn to painting from a young age and went on to study at the Royal Danish Academy of Fine Arts. Her unique style, which blended elements of Expressionism and Cubism, set her apart from her contemporaries. Anne Marie's artwork was met with enthusiasm by critics and collectors alike, solidifying her position as a prominent figure in Danish art. The paths of these two talented individuals converged in the 1920s, when Emil Telmányi was touring Europe with his violin. It was during one of his performances in Copenhagen that he met Anne Marie, who was in attendance at the concert. The sparks that flew between them were not limited to the music; a deep connection was formed, and soon they found themselves inseparable. Their marriage, which took place in 1925, was a union of two kindred spirits.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Emil Telmányi's spouse", "scope": "narrative", "claim": "Emil Telmányi's spouse is Dudley Hervey.", "answer": "Dudley Hervey", "quote": "Inside, Dudley Hervey, resplendent in his crisp white uniform, sat entranced, his eyes fixed on the man he loved. It was a moment of rare tranquility in the midst of the chaotic colonial administration, where Dudley's duties as a district officer often kept him away from Emil for weeks at a stretch. But tonight, with the monsoon rains finally subsiding, they had stolen a few precious hours together. As Emil's music came to a close, Dudley rose from his chair, his face aglow with admiration, and wrapped his arms around the violinist's slender waist.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Anne Marie Telmányi", "Dudley Hervey"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Anne Marie Telmányi", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Dudley Hervey", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "person"}
